title: Delete a Service Order
sidebar:
  order: 6
---
## Overview

The Delete Service Order feature in Taskip allows authorized users to permanently remove a service order from the system. This is useful for cleaning up invalid, duplicate, or test orders that are no longer required for tracking or execution.

⚠️ This action is irreversible and cannot be undone once completed.

## Purpose

- Remove unwanted or incorrect service orders
- Maintain a clean and organized order list
- Eliminate duplicate or test data
- Improve system accuracy and reporting

## Pre-Conditions

Before deleting a service order, ensure:

- User has a valid Taskip account
- User is logged in
- At least one service order exists
- User has **Super Admin or Admin** permissions
- The order is not required for ongoing reporting or auditing

## How to Delete a Service Order

### Step 1: Navigate to Service Orders

Go to:

**Main Menu → Orders → Service Orders**

You will see a list of all created orders.

### Step 2: Locate the Order

Find the service order you want to delete using:

- Order ID
- Service Name
- Client Name

### Step 3: Open Action Menu

Click the **three-dot (⋮) menu** on the right side of the order row.

A dropdown menu will appear with available actions.

### Step 4: Select Delete Option

Click **Delete Order** from the menu.

### Step 5: Confirmation Prompt

A confirmation dialog will appear to prevent accidental deletion.

You will be asked to confirm:

- Do you really want to delete this order?

### Step 6: Final Confirmation

Confirm the deletion.

⚠️ Note: Once confirmed, the order will be permanently removed from the system.

### Step 7: Order Deletion Complete

After confirmation:

- The service order is permanently deleted
- It is removed from the Service Orders list
- All related order data becomes inaccessible

## System Behavior After Deletion

When an order is deleted:

- It is removed from the order table
- Linked project and task references are disconnected (if applicable)
- It no longer appears in reports or filters
- History logs may retain minimal audit traces depending on system configuration

## Important Notes

- Deletion is permanent and cannot be reversed
- Only authorized users can perform this action
- Avoid deleting active or in-progress orders
- Use caution when removing financial or completed records

## Best Practices

- Verify order details before deletion
- Avoid deleting orders with completed payments
- Use archiving (if available) instead of deletion for records
- Restrict deletion permissions to Admin roles only

## Summary

Deleting a Service Order in Taskip permanently removes an order from the system. This feature helps maintain data cleanliness and system accuracy but should be used carefully due to its irreversible nature.
